                <pb facs="0562" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg482"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sickles to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Sickles reports that the consul-general at Barcelona considers it important
                    to know immediately if the Department means by “Cubans and Porto Ricans”
                    resident inhabitants only, or if it means also persons born in those islands,
                    but resident since for some years in Spain.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
